{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Journey Through Japan**\n\nLast month, I embarked on a two-week adventure in Japan, a country where ancient traditions meet cutting-edge modernity. My trip began in Tokyo, where neon lights of Shibuya and Shinjuku dazzled against the backdrop of historic temples like Senso-ji. I indulged in sushi at Tsukiji Outer Market, savored matcha treats in Uji, and navigated the efficient subway system with ease.\n\nA highlight was Kyoto, where I wandered through bamboo groves in Arashiyama and geisha spotting in Gion. The serene Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its thousands of torii gates, left me in awe. I also took a day trip to Nara, feeding the friendly deer in the park and marveling at Todai-ji’s giant Buddha statue.\n\nOsaka’s street food scene stole my heart—takoyaki and okonomiyaki were must-tries. The Dotonbori district pulsated with energy, and Universal Studios Japan’s Super Nintendo World was a playful delight.\n\nFrom the bullet trains’ speed to the meticulous etiquette of ryokans, Japan’s contrasts fascinated me. Whether it was a vending machine coffee at 3 AM or a quiet tea ceremony, every moment felt like a blend of the extraordinary and the everyday.\n\nJapan didn’t just meet my expectations—it exceeded them. I left with a suitcase full of souvenirs, a heart full of memories, and an insatiable urge to return. Would I go back? Absolutely. Next time, I’d explore Hokkaido’s snowy landscapes or dive deeper into the countryside’s hidden gems.\n\nUntil then, *sayōnara* to Japan—see you soon!", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.07776619493961334}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.04390162229537964}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.5959895253181458}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -2.729855441430118e-05}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -1.6549174785614014}, {"token": " Through", "logprob": -0.0360